# W44-223 post-local-butteraugli-patch comprehensive cjxl-parity sweep
# Re-runs the W44-202 4000-cell step-0.25 sweep on commit 399ad8ee (current main)
# after the local-butteraugli patch (commit 399ad8ee) replaced crates.io
# butteraugli 0.9.2 with a workspace path dep to ~/work/zen/butteraugli.
#
# PURPOSE: confirm or refute whether the local-butteraugli patch shifted
# butteraugli scores (which would invalidate the W44-202 Lock-Zenjxl
# baselines locked at 0d5edbfd).
date: 2026-05-23
parent_commit: 399ad8ee710acda621a6a02057ebce3d1d20f10f
working_copy: 44c8be367ca8a3918e67d3d2b62de9e0169cdee5
host: lilith
cjxl_version: cjxl v0.12.0 4279d48 [_AVX3_,AVX2,SSE4,SSE2] {GNU 11.4.0}
manifest: benchmarks/corpora/w44_170_varied_corpus.tsv
corpus_dir: /home/lilith/work/codec-corpus
strategies: ["zenjxl", "libjxl"]
distance_grid: [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 1.75, 2.0, 2.25, 2.5, 2.75, 3.0, 3.25, 3.5, 3.75, 4.0, 4.25, 4.5, 4.75, 5.0]
efforts: [5, 6, 7, 8, 9]
time_iters: 1
smoke: false
wall_seconds: 1518.6
wall_minutes: 25.3
cells_total: 4000
cells_failed: 39
cells_failed_zenjxl: 19
cells_failed_libjxl: 20
cells_ok_zenjxl: 1981
cells_ok_libjxl: 1980
decoder: jxl-oxide (srgb_linear)
metrics: butteraugli_linear (default params, LOCAL butteraugli at ../../butteraugli/butteraugli); fast_ssim2 (sRGB u8 from linear)
tsv_outputs:
  zenjxl: benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_223_zenjxl_2026-05-23.tsv
  libjxl: benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_223_libjxl_2026-05-23.tsv
analysis_text: benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_223_analysis_2026-05-23.txt
lock_cross_check: benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_223_lock_check_2026-05-23.txt
reproducer (full sweep):
  cargo run -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' --example w44_170_cjxl_step025_sweep -- --corpus-manifest benchmarks/corpora/w44_170_varied_corpus.tsv --output-prefix benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_223 --strategies zenjxl,libjxl

# === Aggregate comparison to W44-202 baseline (1978 OK cells per strategy) ===
#   Metric                    W44-202        W44-223        Delta
#   Zenjxl mean delta_bytes_pct  -5.876 %      -6.672 %      -0.80 pp (better)
#   Zenjxl mean delta_ssim2      +0.484        +0.483        -0.001 (unchanged)
#   Zenjxl mean delta_bfly_pct   -6.684 %      -6.706 %      -0.02 pp (unchanged)
#   Zenjxl mean delta_ms_pct     +7.754 %      +34.252 %     +26.5 pp (slower under load)
#   Libjxl mean delta_bytes_pct  +0.756 %      +1.342 %      +0.59 pp
#   Libjxl mean delta_ssim2      -1.945        -1.945        unchanged
#
# === Per-matched-cell diff (n=1978 zenjxl, n=1977 libjxl) ===
#
#   Zenjxl:
#     ours_bytes_diff       mean=-467.120  median=-210.000   (bytes shifted by
#                                                              4 commits between
#                                                              56c9bd80 and 399ad8ee)
#     ours_ssim2_diff       mean=+0.000 median=+0.000        BYTE-IDENTICAL
#     ours_bfly_diff        mean=+0.000 median=+0.000        BYTE-IDENTICAL
#     |ours_bfly_diff|      max=+0.000                       BYTE-IDENTICAL
#     |cjxl_bfly_diff|      max=+0.000                       BYTE-IDENTICAL
#
#   Libjxl:
#     ours_bytes_diff       mean=+0.000 median=+0.000        BYTE-IDENTICAL (Libjxl
#                                                              strategy is byte-locked
#                                                              and W44-T1-T2 work did
#                                                              not change Libjxl path)
#     ours_ssim2_diff       mean=+0.000 median=+0.000        BYTE-IDENTICAL
#     ours_bfly_diff        mean=+0.000 median=+0.000        BYTE-IDENTICAL
#
# === CRITICAL FINDING ===
#
# The local butteraugli is producing the EXACT SAME numerical scores as
# crates.io butteraugli 0.9.2 was producing at the W44-202 baseline.
# Per-matched-cell ours_bfly and cjxl_bfly are byte-identical f64 across
# all 1978 matched OK cells in both strategies.
#
# The alleged "5x shift" that motivated the local-butteraugli patch (per
# the parent task's W44-AUDIT-RECON context) is NOT visible in this
# rebench. The local butteraugli is at numerical parity with crates.io
# 0.9.2 on these inputs at default ButteraugliParams.
#
# === LOCK-ZENJXL TRANSCRIPTION ERROR (separate issue) ===
#
# Several Lock-Zenjxl `base_ours_bfly` and `base_cjxl_bfly` values DO
# NOT match either the W44-202 TSV or the W44-223 TSV — for example,
# `terminal e5 d=1.0` has lock=2.106914 but both TSVs report 0.742616
# (a 2.84x discrepancy). However, `1025469 e5 d=1.0` matches exactly
# (lock=1.411649, TSVs=1.411649).
#
# Pattern (across the 12 locked cells, see lock_check.txt):
#   lock/W202 ratios: min=0.98, max=3.03, mean=1.58
#   lock/W223 ratios: min=0.98, max=3.03, mean=1.58  (identical to W202)
#
# This is NOT a butteraugli version shift (which would produce a UNIFORM
# multiplier across all cells). It is a transcription/source mismatch:
# some cells were transcribed from the W44-202 TSV correctly, others
# were taken from a different measurement source (possibly a different
# bench harness, different ButteraugliParams, or a partial rerun TSV
# that didn't get checked in).
#
# All delta_bytes_pct, delta_ssim2, delta_bfly_pct, delta_ms_pct
# entries in the lock baselines DO correctly match the TSV's delta
# columns — only the absolute base_ours_bfly and base_cjxl_bfly are off.
#
# === RECOMMENDATION ===
#
# RE-BASELINE Lock-Zenjxl by re-extracting all 12 cells from the W44-202
# (or W44-223 — they are byte-identical for ours_bfly / ours_ssim2 /
# cjxl_bfly) TSV. The `delta_*` slack tolerances stay the same; only
# the absolute reference numbers need to match the TSV source-of-truth.
# Suggested patch is fully derivable from
# benchmarks/cjxl_step025_w44_202_zenjxl_2026-05-22.tsv via
# scripts/w44_223_lock_check.py.
